    "background_story": "Justin was a high-powered executive who always seemed to be on the go. His days were filled with back-to-back meetings, conference calls, and endless emails. He was always juggling multiple projects at once, and his plate was perpetually full. Despite his best efforts, Justin found himself constantly playing catch-up, never quite able to stay on top of his workload. His social life suffered as a result, with friends and family often complaining that they never saw him. Justin's apartment was a testament to his overbusy lifestyle, with takeout containers and coffee cups scattered everywhere. One day, while rushing to a meeting, Justin spilled coffee all over his shirt and realized that something had to give. He began to reevaluate his priorities and learned to say no to non-essential tasks, slowly finding a better balance between work and life.",
